{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nupd={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Sharpen the VerifyLeader knowledge entry with the self-vote arming the count. Re-reading raft.go:966-990 shows verifyLeader starts by setting the future's vote count to one for the leader itself, then computes the quorum from the voter set, and then registers the same future on every entry of leaderState.replState, which includes non-voter streams; future.go:274-293 shows each successful vote incrementing that count and completing the future when it reaches the quorum. The consequence is arithmetic: in the three-voter shape the quorum is two, so the leader's own vote plus a single non-voter acknowledgement satisfies it and no other voter is needed. The earlier statement described the registration and the quorum but omitted the self-vote, which is what makes one non-voter sufficient.\\\",\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"533b966489544f45b4fcf14f6edce57f-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n   \\\"statement\\\":\\\"verifyLeader arms the verification with the leader's own vote by setting the future's vote count to one, sizes the quorum with quorumSize, which counts voters only, and then registers that future on every entry of leaderState.replState, which startStopReplication creates for every configured server including non-voters; a successful heartbeat or AppendEntries from any of those streams calls notifyAll(true), whose vote increments the count and completes the verification once it reaches the quorum. With three voters the quorum is two, so the leader plus one non-voter acknowledgement completes a verification that no second voter supported.\\\",\n   \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Leader with at least one non-voter replication stream and fewer reachable voters than the voter quorum.\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"raft_verify_leader\\\",\\\"future_verify_vote\\\",\\\"raft_start_stop_repl\\\",\\\"raft_quorum_size\\\"],\n   \\\"changed_premise\\\":\\\"Adds the self-vote initialisation and its arithmetic consequence: the previous statement said the verification was registered on every stream and completed at a voter-sized quorum, but not that the leader counts itself, which is what lets a single non-voter acknowledgement satisfy a quorum of two.\\\",\n   \\\"affected_uses\\\":[\\\"caa518fff77b418d92e38690c7081bfd-interpretation-0\\\",\\\"64b6f78684b04f8ea393a5827f5457c7-experiment\\\",\\\"5ce028c2f59d4d53947fa0617d774295-interpretation-0\\\"]}\n ]\n}\njson.dump(upd, open('draft/update.json','w'), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\nopen('draft/update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -c \\\"\nimport json,jsonschema\ns=json.load(open('/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run/submission.schema.json'))\nd=json.load(open('/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft/update.json'))\njsonschema.validate(d,s);print('schema OK',list(d))\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
