{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Corrected the VerifyLeader behavior entry after re-reading the verification path. The previous statement described the voter-sized quorum and the registration of the verification on every replication stream, including non-voters, but omitted that verifyLeader first arms the future with the leader's own vote by setting the count to one. With that in place the arithmetic is explicit: in a three-voter configuration the quorum is two, so the leader plus a single non-voter acknowledgement completes a verification that no second voter supported, which is exactly the shape all the receipts exercise. The update states the self-vote initialisation, the voter-only quorum, the registration on every stream, and the increment-and-complete behaviour of the future, and records the changed premise and the three affected uses: the current interpretation, the lease experiment and the preceding interpretation. Source identifiers are the ones already registered for the verification path, the quorum helper, the replication stream setup and the future, and the submission validates against submission.schema.json.\"}"}}
